   "line": [
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The Nimzowitsch Sicilian — the knight to f6 on move two. It flies under the radar and looks dubious, but it's a semi-legitimate line worth knowing.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "the Nimzowitsch Sicilian"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 5,
   "t": 61,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp1ppppp/5n2/2p1P3/8/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 3",
   "line": [
    "e5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The reason it looks shaky is e5, hitting the knight — but this simply transposes into an improved Alapin, with the extra pawn on c5 working in our favor.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "...Nf6 e5 = an improved Alapin"
   ]
  },
